## 3️⃣ Use an OkHttp interceptor (if you already have an OkHttp client)

MapLibre’s default HTTP stack is built on **OkHttp**. You can replace the client globally and answer any request that matches a predicate.

```kotlin
import okhttp3.OkHttpClient
import okhttp3.Protocol
import okhttp3.Response
import okhttp3.ResponseBody.Companion.toResponseBody
import org.maplibre.android.module.http.HttpRequestUtil

val client = OkHttpClient.Builder()
    .addInterceptor { chain ->
        val request = chain.request()
        // Detect our custom scheme – we can’t parse it with HttpUrl, so look at the raw string.
        val urlString = request.url.toString()
        if (!urlString.startsWith("vault://")) {
            // Not ours → let OkHttp handle it normally.
            return@addInterceptor chain.proceed(request)
        }

        // Parse z/x/y from the URL.
        val parts = urlString.removePrefix("vault://tiles/").split('/')
        val (z, x, y) = parts.map { it.toInt() }

        // Decrypt the tile.
        val bytes = Vault.decryptTile(z, x, y)

        // Build a synthetic 200 response.
        Response.Builder()
            .request(request)
            .protocol(Protocol.HTTP_1_1)
            .code(200)
            .message("OK")
            .body(bytes.toResponseBody())   // MIME type is ignored; MapLibre treats it as MVT.
            .build()
    }
    .build()

// Tell MapLibre to use this client.
HttpRequestUtil.setOkHttpClient(client)
```

**Important notes**

* The interceptor runs **after** MapLibre has already parsed the URL with `HttpUrl`. `vault://` is *not* a valid URL for `HttpUrl`, so the request will be dropped **before** it reaches the interceptor unless you first replace the scheme with something OkHttp can parse (e.g. `https://vault/…`) and then detect it via a query parameter or a custom host.  
* The more reliable way is the **ModuleProvider** approach (method 1) because it receives the raw `resourceUrl` string *before* any URL parsing.

---

## 🎯 Which method should you pick?

| Situation | Best choice |
|-----------|-------------|
| **You already have a style JSON that uses `vault://…` and you want zero changes** | **Method 1 – custom `HttpRequest` via `ModuleProvider`** |
| **You are comfortable building the source in code and don’t mind moving layer definitions out of JSON** | **Method 2 – `CustomVectorSource`** |
| **Your app already uses OkHttp for other networking and you want a single place to intercept** | **Method 3 – OkHttp interceptor** (but remember the URL-parsing limitation) |

All three approaches are supported from **android-v11.0.0** (ModuleProvider & OkHttp) and **android-v13.5.0** (CustomVectorSource). If you are on an older Android release of MapLibre, upgrade to at least **v13.7.1** to get the latest bug-fixes and the `interpolate-hcl`/`interpolate-lab` parity, but the custom-protocol handling works on any version ≥ 11.0.0.

