## 4️⃣ Quick checklist – did you miss anything?

| ✅ | Item |
|----|------|
| **✅** | `MapLibre.setModuleProvider(...)` called **once** before any `MapView` is created. |
| **✅** | Your `Vault.decryptTile(z, x, y)` returns **exactly** the raw MVT bytes (no extra wrapper, no gzip unless you also set `Content-Encoding`). |
| **✅** | You call `responder.onResponse(200, …, tileBytes)` **on the same thread** that `executeRequest` was called (the native core expects a synchronous callback). |
| **✅** | If you need caching, you can add an `ETag` or `Cache-Control` header in the responder; otherwise leave them `null`. |
| **✅** | The style JSON uses the same `vault://tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}` pattern everywhere (tiles, sprite, glyphs, …) – any URL that you do **

