## 5️⃣  Common pitfalls & how to avoid them

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| **Map shows a blank layer** | The protocol handler never calls `callback` (e.g., you forgot `return` after `callback`). | Ensure every code path ends with `callback(null, …)` **or** `callback(error, null)`. |
| **`[ParseStyle]` errors about “value must be a string”** | You returned a plain `Uint8Array` instead of an `ArrayBuffer`. | Use `response.arrayBuffer()` or `new Uint8Array(...).buffer`. |
| **Tiles are fetched on every pan/zoom** | You never store the tile in IndexedDB, or you store it under a different key. | Verify that `db.putTile(z, x, y, arrayBuffer)` runs and that the key format (`${z}/${x}/${y}`) matches the read logic. |
| **`cache://` URLs are blocked by CORS** | The network fetch (`https://my.tileserver.com/...`) does not allow cross-origin requests. | Add appropriate CORS headers on the tile server, or proxy the request through your own server. |
| **`addProtocol` throws “protocol already registered”** | You called `addProtocol('cache', …)` more than once (e.g., on hot-module reload). | Guard the registration: `if (!maplibregl.getProtocol('cache')) { … }` or place the call in a module that runs only once. |
| **iOS Safari “Failed to fetch”** | Safari’s IndexedDB quota is exhausted. | Periodically prune old tiles (`delete` on the object store) or use the `Cache` API instead of IndexedDB. |

---

