### 3-b️⃣  Adding the source in code (useful if you want to switch URLs at runtime)

```ts
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: {
    version: 8,
    sources: {},
    layers: [],
  },
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2,
});

map.on('style.load', () => {
  // Add the vector source that points to our custom scheme
  map.addSource('my-vector', {
    type: 'vector',
    tiles: ['cache://tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}'],
    minzoom: 0,
    maxzoom: 14,
  });

  // Add a layer that uses the source
  map.addLayer({
    id: 'my-fill',
    type: 'fill',
    source: 'my-vector',
    'source-layer': 'my_layer_name',
    paint: {
      'fill-color': '#88c0d0',
      'fill-opacity': 0.6,
    },
  });
});
```

> **Tip:** If you need to change the remote URL later (e.g., switch between production and staging), just update the `tiles` array and call `map.getSource('my-vector').setTiles([...])`. The `cache://` handler stays the same.

